    "_note": "Deity-names are the Mayan morphs of the Agrippan canon (family_mesoamerican.json theonym_sets.mayan) - never real Maya gods (no Itzamna, Kukulkan, Chaac, Ix Chel, Kinich Ahau). Shared pantheon, Maya names. Ixalan seeds/shifts Lawful or Neutral; its stance follows its CURRENT alignment (see worship_by_alignment). The Long-Count calendar and the bloodletting-rite bind the k'uhul ajaw to the powers; the witz (pyramid) is the altar.",
